            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0660" n="611" xml:id="pg611"/>

                <head>280. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger) to Secretary
                    of State Rogers and Secretary
                    of Defense Laird<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d280-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-01-21">January 21, 1970</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>
                        MAP Alternatives for Indonesia</item>
                </list>
                <p>At the Review Group Meeting on December 22, 1969,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d280-f2"/>
                    it was agreed that the Departments of State and Defense would prepare a
                    memorandum for the President spelling out in broad terms the equipment which
                    would be supplied under the military aid program for Indonesia, under Options 3
                    and 4 of Section VI B of NSSM 61.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d280-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>The consensus in the Review Group was that the program should be somewhat larger
                    than at present and that there should be a judicious addition of combat
                    equipment to the present program, which is limited to civil action
                    equipment.</p>
                <p>The President believes that his conversations with President Suharto oblige him to proceed with a
                    combat/civil action mix, between Options 3 and 4. For planning purposes a
                    program level of about $15 million should be assumed. (If supplies are available
                    from surplus stocks, they could of course be utilized, reducing somewhat the
                    need for additional MAP appropriations.)</p>
                <p>The report to the President should be submitted by February 2.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d280-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">
                            Henry A. Kissinger
                        </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
